@page
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}
<h1> About Us </h1>

<h2>Your fitness, all in one place.</h2>
<p>Pulse is a subscription-based fitness tracker built to help you understand your habits and reach your goals. Instead of juggling a food app, a workout notebook, and a goals list, Pulse brings everything together so you can see the full picture of your health in one dashboard.</p>
<br>
<h2>What You Can Track</h2>
<p>Meals. Log what you eat throughout the day and keep an eye on calories and macronutrients. Over time, you'll see how your nutrition lines up with your training and your goals.</p>
<br>
<p>Workouts. Record each session, whether it's a gym day, a run, a bike ride, or a yoga class. Note the date, duration, and how it went, and build a history you can look back on.</p>
<br>
<p>Exercises. Go deeper than "I worked out." Track individual exercises with sets, reps, weight, distance, or time, so you can watch your strength and endurance improve week over week.</p>
<br>
<p>Goals. Set targets that matter to you, like hitting a new personal record, reaching a weight goal, or working out four times a week, and follow your progress as you get closer.</p>
<br>
<h2>Why Subscribe?</h2>    
<p>A Pulse subscription gives you full access to every tracking feature, your complete history, and progress charts that show how far you've come. Your subscription supports an ad-free experience, so you can stay focused on your training without distractions, and we never sell your data. (See our Privacy Statement for details.)</p>
<br>
<h2>Our Mission</h2>
<p>We believe progress comes from consistency, and consistency comes from seeing your effort pay off. Pulse is designed to make tracking simple enough that you'll actually stick with it, and insightful enough that it keeps you motivated.</p>
<br>
<h2>Who We Are</h2>
<p>Pulse was created by our group as a project for Programming and Modern Framework at the University of Cincinnati. We built it with ASP.NET Core Razor Pages because we wanted to create something we'd actually want to use ourselves.<p>


